WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.819
I've spoken to you before about different
ways in which the world really has been laughing

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:09.670
at us for a long time since Donald Trump became
president.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:15.639
They laughed when we elected a president who
thinks climate change is a Chinese hoax.

00:00:15.639 --> 00:00:22.160
They laughed that we elected a president who
has no idea how economics or currency or trade

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:27.280
or medicine or the constitution or the law
or public transit or any of it works.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.170
And they were laughing at us early during
the Corona virus pandemic.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:36.129
And even as recently as a couple of weeks
ago, many countries were laughing at us.

00:00:36.129 --> 00:00:40.899
I showed you about 10 days ago articles from
all over the world, the Netherlands, South

00:00:40.899 --> 00:00:46.629
Africa, Peru, everywhere, ridiculing our moronic
president for his comments about bleach, injections

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:50.239
and the other things he said during that press
briefing.

00:00:50.239 --> 00:00:52.950
But they're not really laughing anymore.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:57.980
Now it has gone from laughter to concern to
actual pity.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:03.180
The emails I have gotten over the last few
days from our international viewers, people

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:09.461
that used to be poking fun at Trump's idiotic
claims about vaccines and the virus, they

00:01:09.461 --> 00:01:14.340
now write to me and say, David, we feel sorry
for you that you were dealing with this in

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.830
the United States.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:22.360
We feel sorry that you are in a situation
where no matter what you do, even if you do

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:27.160
the right things, even if you have the best
intentions and the accurate understanding

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:31.720
of what it is that's going on and what it
is that's necessary to deal with this virus,

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:35.870
we feel sorry for you because your federal
government has failed.

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.320
They are incompetent.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.090
There is no plan.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:46.530
There is just a series of lies and disinformation
and confusion and bogus talking points.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:51.090
And there are even Republicans who are willing
to tell the truth.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.300
They are increasingly agreeing this is just
some Republicans.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.710
Of course, most of them are actually behind
Donald Trump.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:00.690
Check out Republican strategist Steve Schmidt
explaining it again.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.350
This is a lifelong Republican strategists.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:03.350
Take it.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.350
Take a look.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:08.830
Donald Trump has been the worst president
this country has ever had.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:14.099
And I don't say that hyperbolic heat here.

00:02:14.099 --> 00:02:15.099
But here's a consequential president.

00:02:15.099 --> 00:02:22.519
And he has brought this country in three short
years to a place of weakness that is simply

00:02:22.519 --> 00:02:24.439
unimaginable.

00:02:24.439 --> 00:02:31.299
If you were pondering where we are today from
the day where Barack Obama left office and

00:02:31.299 --> 00:02:36.430
there were a lot of us on that day who were
deeply skeptical and very worried about what

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:42.400
a Trump presidency would be.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:51.480
But this is a moment of unparalleled national
humiliation, of weakness.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.180
When you listen to the president, these are
the musings of an imbecile, an idiot.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:54.180
And I don't use those words.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:57.099
The name call, I use them because they're
the precise words in the English language

00:02:57.099 --> 00:03:03.129
to describe his behavior, his comportment,
his actions.

00:03:03.129 --> 00:03:09.189
We've never seen a level of incompetence,
a level of ineptitude so staggering on a daily

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:18.019
basis by anybody in the history of the country
whose ever been charged with substantial responsibility.

00:03:18.019 --> 00:03:21.189
Steve Schmidt, Schmidt is sadly absolutely
right.

00:03:21.189 --> 00:03:23.139
The presidency is deadly.

00:03:23.139 --> 00:03:29.290
And as more and more countries open up, it
is us people in the United States who won't

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:33.930
be allowed to fly into other countries because
we are a mess here as other countries are

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:39.249
actually dealing with the problem as Trump
talks about a super duper missile.

00:03:39.249 --> 00:03:40.249
We'll get to that later.

00:03:40.249 --> 00:03:42.540
That's actually a phrase that he used.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:47.480
His son goes on TV and says it's all going
to disappear on Election Day because it's

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:50.750
merely a fake political scandal by Democrats.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:58.609
As that goes on here, the world is taking
pity on us for our failed leadership.

00:03:58.609 --> 00:04:07.099
I was trying over the weekend to think of
an analogy to try to apply to this, because

00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:13.409
there are people who are analyzing this administration
as if it were a normal administration.

00:04:13.409 --> 00:04:18.190
You have these people, some of whom are so-called
enlightened centrists, who pretend to see

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:23.349
both sides and find things they like and Trump
and things that they dislike.

00:04:23.349 --> 00:04:27.169
You can't evaluate this president like you
can other presidents.

00:04:27.169 --> 00:04:31.169
Here's an analogy I thought of that I'm workshopping
and I want to try out on you.

00:04:31.169 --> 00:04:36.979
When someone says about Trump, well, you know,
he has an unusual way of talking about the

00:04:36.979 --> 00:04:37.979
issues.

00:04:37.979 --> 00:04:42.300
But he's right on de-regulation and he's right
on trade.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.970
But maybe he's not the best guy on Corona
virus.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:45.970
Imagine.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.610
OK, this is the analogy.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:52.720
Imagine I was playing in a chess tournament
and I show up and I replace all the queen,

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:58.199
the pawns on the board with Queens that I
take out of my pocket before the game starts.

00:04:58.199 --> 00:04:59.530
That's insane.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:03.180
And it's simultaneously making a mockery of
the tournament.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:04.460
It's also cheating.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:07.710
I'm also either an idiot or a bad person for
doing it.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:12.669
Imagine that a chess commentator sees me take
eight queens out of my pocket and put him

00:05:12.669 --> 00:05:17.621
on the board instead of the pawns and says,
you know, David, strategy is unusual, but

00:05:17.621 --> 00:05:20.310
it's certainly an aggressive way to play the
game.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:21.310
What?

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:22.310
No.

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:23.310
That doesn't make sense.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.310
Yeah.

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:28.990
I mean, some players use the Spanish opening
and others take Queens out of their pocket

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:30.270
and replace the ponds.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.550
We're not talking about the same thing here.

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:37.659
So when these enlightened centrists and pragmatic
conservatives and whoever else, when they

00:05:37.659 --> 00:05:43.400
pretend to do an analysis of Donald Trump's
presidency as if it were even remotely normal,

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.710
they're failing the sniff test on principle.

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:52.410
But there's another issue here, with very
few exceptions in the Republican Party.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:54.669
They are mostly just enabling this.

00:05:54.669 --> 00:05:59.610
There are a few Republicans who have taken
a stand and are saying this can't happen.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:00.610
Right.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:04.199
You've got people like Mitt Romney, who's
a current senator from Utah, Republican.

00:06:04.199 --> 00:06:06.800
You have George Conway, a lifelong Republican.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.240
Steve Schmidt, lifelong Republican strategist.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:14.569
There are a few other Republicans I can't
name them all, who have not softened their

00:06:14.569 --> 00:06:15.810
view on Trump.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:18.550
And they are straight up saying this is not
acceptable.

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:19.910
This is not normal.

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:25.730
This can't be dealt with in normal terms because
normal terms don't apply.

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.759
I'm not talking about them.

00:06:27.759 --> 00:06:33.569
But for the most part, Republicans in Congress,
in the House and Senate have enabled this.

00:06:33.569 --> 00:06:35.740
Most Republican governors have enabled this.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:38.850
So Trump is not alone to blame here.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:44.660
We have to blame the sixty three million Americans
that voted for Donald Trump.

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:45.860
Yes, they are to blame.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:51.120
It doesn't matter whether you call them bad
people or stupid or they are to blame.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:54.629
Their actions are to blame for what we are
dealing with right now.

00:06:54.629 --> 00:06:57.250
Of course, Trump is to blame.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:03.599
But the Republican Party, that mostly continues
to enable him that even before the impeachment

00:07:03.599 --> 00:07:08.600
trial had already decided were voting to acquit
Donald Trump on impeachment charges.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.970
They have to be held accountable as well.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:15.090
We have the opportunity to hold every single
one of the Republicans in the House accountable

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:16.110
in November.

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:21.129
We have an opportunity to hold the Republicans
that are up for reelection in the Senate in

00:07:21.129 --> 00:07:23.189
November, which is of the 34 up for reelection.

00:07:23.189 --> 00:07:28.090
I forget the exact number of Republicans,
but a number of Republicans are up for reelection

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.110
in November.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:08:21.139
They have to be held accountable

00:08:21.139 --> 00:08:54.400
as well.

